      "content": "interesting. so you're saying the opposition is basically just being stuck in the past? it feels like you're dismissing pretty big economic concerns as just being \"fear-based.\" even if productivity goes up, wouldn't the transition period be a complete mess for most people? is there any legitimate economic reasoning for the skeptics, or is it pretty much a settled issue at this point?",
